<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-4335] Deleting a Notebook is vulnerable to XSS attach</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-4335</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Problem Statement : Deleting a Notebook is vulnerable to XSS attach&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Issue reproducing :&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1) create a notebook&lt;br/&gt;
2) give the permission to notebook as : &amp;lt;script&amp;gt;alert(&apos;hi&apos;)&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt; (press space after writing this, not enter key)&lt;br/&gt;
3) after this, try to delete the notebook, the BootstrapDialog that popups stating insufficient privilages is vulnerable to XSS attack&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;analysis : &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/dda5a145249538eb5a49e452e34f9c5779e0ad87/zeppelin-web/src/components/websocket/websocket-event.factory.js#L110&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/dda5a145249538eb5a49e452e34f9c5779e0ad87/zeppelin-web/src/components/websocket/websocket-event.factory.js#L110&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;in thi part of code we should sanitize the input given to bootStrapDialog with _.escape&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
